  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 227 PM CDT Fri Aug 7 2026\n\nHot Saturday through Tuesday:\n\nTemperatures will increase on Saturday into early next week as a\nridge axis shifts east and heights increase over the area.\nNBM dewpoints are currently in the low 70s, though a look at \nforecast soundings suggests afternoon mixing may knock them \ntown a touch. Regardless, with temperatures in the 90s, \nconditions will feel quite hot. Afternoon heat indices are \nforecast to climb into the 100 to 105 deg range each day. We \nhave held off on any headline issuance for now given the \nmarginal heat indices, but if confidence in locations reaching \n105 degrees any given day or multiple days of 100+ increases, \nthen a Heat Advisory may be warranted.\n\nRain Chances Return Late Next Week:\n\nGlobal ensembles depict the aforementioned ridge flattening by\nWednesday. This will open the door to the return of\nprecipitation chances with any shortwave passage. Current NBM\nPoPs are in the 30-60% range Wednesday into the end of the week.\nThe CPC gives us a 40-50% chance for seeing above normal \nprecipitation between August 12-16. Since normal precipitation \nfor this time period is around 0.5-0.75 inches, there is a \n40-50% chance for exceeding that amount between August 12-16.",
